  "notes": "{近|ちか}づく means to approach, either physically or in terms of time.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {近|ちか}づける (transitive, to bring close)\n\nPATTERN:\nXに{近|ちか}づく: to approach X, get close to X\n\nTWO MAIN USES:\n1. Physical approach: {駅|えき}に{近|ちか}づく (approach the station)\n2. Time approaching: {夏|なつ}が{近|ちか}づく (summer is approaching)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {危険|きけん}に{近|ちか}づくな: Don't approach the danger\n- {締|し}め{切|き}りが{近|ちか}づいている: The deadline is approaching\n- もっと{近|ちか}づいて: Come closer\n\nNEGATIVE WARNING:\n〜に{近|ちか}づくな is a common warning meaning \"don't go near ~.\"",
